00:05:21,318 --> 00:05:25,873
"Commit suggestion"; here, the same change as a commit):

72
00:05:27,633 --> 00:05:29,810
Let me try something.

73
00:05:29,810 --> 00:05:31,883
Approve your own PR:

74
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:35,178
Can not approve your own pull request:

75
00:05:35,178 --> 00:05:37,778
a review is a second person's check.

76
00:05:37,778 --> 00:05:45,144
GitHub does not count the author, and "request changes" on your own PR is refused for the same reason.

77
00:05:45,144 --> 00:05:48,755
If a repository requires one approval (lesson 59),

78
00:05:48,755 --> 00:05:53,883
a PR cannot be merged until someone else with write access approves it.

79
00:05:55,633 --> 00:06:04,017
Ask a reviewer (gh pr edit price-green-tea --add-reviewer TEAMMATE, or "Reviewers" on the PR page).

80
00:06:04,017 --> 00:06:07,743
The reviewer, logged in as themselves, runs:

81
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:10,213
Got it.

82
00:06:10,213 --> 00:06:12,965
What do I need to remember?

83
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,838
Review verdicts:

84
00:06:14,838 --> 00:06:21,615
comment, approve, request changes; line comments can carry one-click suggestions.

85
00:06:22,167 --> 00:06:26,696
The author answers by pushing commits; the PR updates.

86
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:29,683
Nobody can approve their own PR:

87
00:06:29,683 --> 00:06:32,593
required reviews need a second person.

88
00:06:34,333 --> 00:06:36,918
Why would I need merge strategies?

89
00:06:37,467 --> 00:06:40,332
GitHub's merge button has three modes:

90
00:06:40,332 --> 00:06:44,706
Create a merge commit, Squash and merge, Rebase and merge.

91
00:06:44,706 --> 00:06:47,722
Each leaves a different history on main.

92
00:06:47,722 --> 00:06:53,076
We reproduce all three locally to see the graphs, then merge a real PR.

93
00:06:54,833 --> 00:06:59,233
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

94
00:06:59,767 --> 00:07:03,709
Create a merge commit (GitHub always uses --no-ff here):

95
00:07:03,709 --> 00:07:04,906
Squash and merge:

96
00:07:04,906 --> 00:07:08,496
the branch's changes become one new commit on main:

97
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:10,253
Squash and merge:

98
00:07:10,253 --> 00:07:13,910
the branch's changes become one new commit on main:

99
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:15,130
Rebase and merge:

100
00:07:15,130 --> 00:07:19,433
the commits replayed on top of main, without a merge commit:

101
00:07:19,967 --> 00:07:21,246
Rebase and merge:

102
