the commits replayed on top of main, without a merge commit:

103
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:29,146
Same files on all three, different histories:

104
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,633
Let me try something.

105
00:07:32,633 --> 00:07:37,915
After a squash merge, delete the PR branch locally the safe way:

106
00:07:38,467 --> 00:07:38,883
error:

107
00:07:38,883 --> 00:07:41,866
the branch 'pr-squash' is not fully merged:

108
00:07:41,866 --> 00:07:47,277
Git checks whether the branch's commits are reachable from the current branch.

109
00:07:47,277 --> 00:07:52,272
After a squash they are not (the content is, inside a different commit).

110
00:07:52,272 --> 00:07:54,076
Check the content instead:

111
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:57,165
Content verified:

112
00:07:57,165 --> 00:07:58,340
delete with -D.

113
00:07:58,340 --> 00:08:05,938
On GitHub, enable "Automatically delete head branches" so merged PR branches are deleted for you.

114
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:08,413
Got it.

115
00:08:08,413 --> 00:08:11,165
What do I need to remember?

116
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:12,960
Merge commit:

117
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:17,127
keeps everything + the PR boundary; squash:

118
00:08:17,127 --> 00:08:19,646
one commit per PR; rebase:

119
00:08:19,646 --> 00:08:21,585
linear, all commits.

120
00:08:22,133 --> 00:08:27,852
After squash/rebase merges, git branch -d says "not fully merged":

121
00:08:27,852 --> 00:08:30,018
compare content, then -D.

122
00:08:30,567 --> 00:08:34,176
Configure the allowed strategies per repository.
